{"success": true, "message": "Test details sent successfully", "data": {"test": {"_id": "69de21ea7e39d99b57bc5a9e", "analysisVideoCdn": "yt", "exam": ["605dfcb2f226ac25a8bd5fef"], "ctype": null, "position": 0, "order": 12, "enableCalculator": false, "isContinuousQuestion": false, "reattemptAvailable": false, "singleSectionMultipleSubjects": false, "timeRestricted": false, "title": "Work, Power and Energy - Test 3", "description": "Previous Year Questions as Chapter Test", "syllabus": "This test contains questions from all topics of this chapter included in the JEE Main syllabus. It includes a mix of questions from PYQs of JEE Main 2019 - 2025.", "totalTime": 50, "totalQuestions": 25, "totalMarks": 100, "bonusQuestions": null, "bonusMarks": null, "startDate": "2026-04-15T03:30:00.000Z", "endDate": "2027-04-30T00:00:00.000Z", "type": "free", "class": "605df635a37b7025c438d685", "instruction": "608289ffb160b022e9442c83", "subjects": [{"subjectId": "607018ee404ae53194e73d90", "totalMarks": 100, "bonusMarks": 0, "totalQuestions": 25, "bonusQuestions": 0, "_id": "69de4f502ee0e063d926831a"}], "sections": [{"sectionId": {"_id": "69de4f502ee0e063d92682d1", "title": "Physics Single Correct", "sectionType": "normal", "subject": "607018ee404ae53194e73d90", "questions": [{"_id": "69de4f502ee0e063d926826a", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0dfaa"], "topics": ["60e40fd5f1ef260f84ed1e96"], "concepts": ["60e567aa499d1e49588f95c3"], "question": {"text": "A force $\\mathrm{F}=\\alpha+\\beta \\mathrm{x}^2$ acts on an object in the x -direction. The work done by the force is 5 J when the object is displaced by 1 m . If the constant $\\alpha=1 \\mathrm{~N}$ then $\\beta$ will be"}, "options": [{"id": "4b1f3c", "text": "$15 \\mathrm{~N} / \\mathrm{m}^2$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f502ee0e063d926826b"}, {"id": "9a7c5e", "text": "$12 \\mathrm{~N} / \\mathrm{m}^2$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f502ee0e063d926826c"}, {"id": "0c8df8", "text": "$8 \\mathrm{~N} / \\mathrm{m}^2$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f502ee0e063d926826d"}, {"id": "221ff4", "text": "$10 \\mathrm{~N} / \\mathrm{m}^2$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f502ee0e063d926826e"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f502ee0e063d926826f", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0dfaa"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b476b"], "concepts": ["6117b8bd67dbe2603c3e85b3"], "question": {"text": "<p>A bob of mass <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>m</mi></math> is suspended by a light string of length <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>L</mi></math>. It is imparted a minimum horizontal velocity at the lowest point <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math> such that it just completes half circle reaching the top most position <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi></math>. The ratio of kinetic energies <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mo>(</mo><mo> </mo><mi>K</mi><mo>.</mo><mi>E</mi><mo>. </mo><msub><mo>)</mo><mi>A</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mo> </mo><mi>K</mi><mo>.</mo><mi>E</mi><mo>. </mo><msub><mo>)</mo><mi>B</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></math> is :</p><img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2F70faeffc-7541-4ec4-b7b9-e636d94cd0d0.png?alt=media\" style=\"width: 250px; height: 263px;\"/>"}, "options": [{"id": "f0353e", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><mo>:</mo><mn>2</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f502ee0e063d9268270"}, {"id": "b47975", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn><mo>:</mo><mn>1</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f502ee0e063d9268271"}, {"id": "bbe3de", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>:</mo><mn>5</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f502ee0e063d9268272"}, {"id": "b6e7ac", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>:</mo><mn>5</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f502ee0e063d9268273"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f502ee0e063d9268274", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0dfaa"], "topics": ["60e2fb1f66f9ce3f243b4b68"], "concepts": ["60e40fd4f1ef260f84ed1e3f"], "question": {"text": "A particle of mass <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>m</mi></math>&nbsp;is moving in a circular path of constant radius <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>r</mi></math>&nbsp;such that its centripetal acceleration <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>c</mi></msub></math> is varying with time <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>t</mi></math>&nbsp;as <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>k</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>r</mi><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math> , where <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>k</mi></math>&nbsp;is a constant. The power delivered to the particle by the force acting on it is -"}, "options": [{"id": "050456", "text": "Zero", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f502ee0e063d9268275"}, {"id": "f402e5", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mi>m</mi><msup><mi>k</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>t</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f502ee0e063d9268276"}, {"id": "9c19b6", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>m</mi><msup><mi>k</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>t</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f502ee0e063d9268277"}, {"id": "70ff8c", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mi>m</mi><msup><mi>k</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>r</mi><mi>t</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f502ee0e063d9268278"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f502ee0e0