/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo> </mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mfenced></math></p><img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2F9c784420-fc7d-47bb-8680-70c16514ab42.png?alt=media\" style=\"width: 200px; height: 188px;\"/>"}, "options": [{"id": "25089c", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f502ee0e063d926827f"}, {"id": "6d185a", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f502ee0e063d9268280"}, {"id": "bb9046", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn><mo>×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>3</mn></msup><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f502ee0e063d9268281"}, {"id": "7bb608", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>10</mn><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f502ee0e063d9268282"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f502ee0e063d9268283", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0dfaa"], "topics": ["60e2fb1f66f9ce3f243b4b68"], "concepts": ["60e2fb1f66f9ce3f243b4b2b"], "question": {"text": "An object of mass 1000 g experiences a time dependent force $\\vec{F}=\\left(2 t \\hat{i}+3 t^2 \\hat{j}\\right) N$. The power generated by the force at time $t$ is :"}, "options": [{"id": "20d774", "text": "$\\left(2 t^2+3 t^3\\right) W$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f502ee0e063d9268284"}, {"id": "9d1bf5", "text": "$\\left(2 t^2+18 t^3\\right) W$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f502ee0e063d9268285"}, {"id": "1d2373", "text": "$\\left(3 t^3+5 t^5\\right) W$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f502ee0e063d9268286"}, {"id": "e4c762", "text": "$\\left(2 t^3+3 t^5\\right) W$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f502ee0e063d9268287"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f502ee0e063d9268288", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0dfaa"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b476b"], "concepts": ["60e2fbdc66f9ce3f243b564c"], "question": {"text": "A particle of mass <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>m</mi></math> moves in a circular orbit&nbsp;under the central potential field, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>U</mi><mfenced><mi>r</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo>-</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><mi>r</mi></mfrac></math>,&nbsp;where <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>C</mi></math> is a positive constant. The correct radius - velocity graph of the particle&#39;s motion is :"}, "options": [{"id": "6e57a0", "text": "<img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2Fbe2e85fe-3ee4-4128-86f7-6846a1520a37-image.png?alt=media\" style=\"width: 160px; height: 131px;\" />", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f502ee0e063d9268289"}, {"id": "6e61fb", "text": "<img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2F9b354441-7a41-454a-9f38-65fdad946ec7-image.png?alt=media\" style=\"width: 162px; height: 126px;\" />", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f502ee0e063d926828a"}, {"id": "02f629", "text": "<img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2F4233aae4-6de2-4e9d-9140-176dd023492a-image.png?alt=media\" style=\"width: 160px; height: 133px;\" />", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f502ee0e063d926828b"}, {"id": "278524", "text": "<img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2F85cb04ae-97e9-4a9c-9b8e-366b136901d4-image.png?alt=media\" style=\"width: 162px; height: 132px;\" />", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f502ee0e063d926828c"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f502ee0e063d926828d", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0dfaa"], "topics": ["60e40fd5f1ef260f84ed1e96"], "concepts": ["60e40fd4f1ef260f84ed1e3c"], "question": {"text": "A particle of mass <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>500</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></math> is moving in a straight line with velocity <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>v</mi><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">b</mi><msup><mi>x</mi><mfrac><mn>5</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></msup></math>. The work done by the net force during its displacement from <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>&nbsp;to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math> is &nbsp;(Take <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">b</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>25</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></mrow><mfrac><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></msup><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>)."}, "options": [{"id": "fc23de", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f502ee0e063d926828e"}, {"id": "d79f73", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f502ee0e063d926828f"}, {"id": "c81abd", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>8</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f502ee0e063d9268290"}, {"id": "7d04d0", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>16</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f502ee0e063d9268291"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f502ee0e063d9268292", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0dfaa"], "topics": ["60e2fb1f66f9ce3f243b4b68"], "concepts": ["60e5671a499d1e49588f87c4"], "question": {"text": "Water falls from a <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>40</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math> high dam at the rate of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>9</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>4</mn></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>kg</mi></math> per hour. Fifty percentage of gravitational potential energy can be converted into electrical energy. Using this hydro electric energy number of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>100</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">W</mi></math> lamps, that can be lit, is<br />(Take <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>g</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn><msup><mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>ms</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></math>)"}, "options": [{"id": "140ba6", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>25</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f502ee0e063d9268293"}, {"id": "4b8afd", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>50</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f502ee0e063d9268294"}, {"id": "cd189f", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>100</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f502ee0e063d9268295"}, {"id": "3db0b4", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>18</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f502ee0e063d9268296"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f502ee0e063d9268297", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0dfaa"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b476b"], "concepts": ["60e2fb5666f9ce3f243b4f00"], "question": {"text": "<p>A particle is placed at the point <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math> of a frictionless track <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>ABC</mi></math> as shown in figure. It is gently pushed towards right. The speed of the particle when it reaches the point <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi></math> is: <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo></math>Take <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced open=\"\"><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo> </mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mfenced></math>.</p><img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2F9b179c38-6291-497f-abe6-f036b3493e88.png?alt=media\" style=\"width: 400px; height: 147px;\"/>"}, "options": [{"id": "3d28b8", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>20</mn><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo> </mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f502ee0e063d9268298"}, {"id": "c576a2", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msqrt><mn>10</mn></msqrt><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo> </mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f502ee0e063d9268299"}, {"id": "d3f039", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><msqrt><mn>10</mn></msqrt><mo> </mo><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo> </mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f502ee0e063d926829a"}, {"id": "8702c7", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>10</mn><mo> </mo><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo> </mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f502ee0e063d926829b"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f502ee0e063d926829c", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0dfaa"], "topics": ["60e2fb1f66f9ce3f243b4b68"], "concepts": ["60e40fd4f1ef260f84ed1e3f"], "question": {"text": "A body of mass 4 kg is placed on a plane at a point P having coordinate $(3,4) \\mathrm{m}$. Under the action of force $\\overrightarrow{\\mathrm{F}}=(2 \\hat{i}+3 \\hat{j}) \\mathrm{N}$, it moves to a new point Q having coordinates $(6,10) \\mathrm{m}$ in 4 sec . The average power and instanteous power at the end of 4 sec are in the ratio of :"}, "options": [{"id": "40ae1d", "text": "$13: 6$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f502ee0e063d926829d"}, {"id": "83f5c4", "text": "$4: 3$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f502ee0e063d926829e"}, {"id": "e6a223", "text": "$1: 2$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f502ee0e063d926829f"}, {"id": "922316", "text": "$6: 13$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f502ee0e063d92682a0"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f502ee0e063d92682a1", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0dfaa"], "topics": ["60e40fd5f1ef260f84ed1e96"], "concepts": ["60e567aa499d1e49588f95c3"], "question": {"text": "A particle of mass $m$ moves on a straight line with its velocity increasing with distance according to the equation $v=\\alpha \\sqrt{x}$, where $\\alpha$ is a constant. The total work done by all the forces applied on the particle during its displacement from $x=0$ to $x=\\mathrm{d}$, will be :"}, "options": [{"id": "b1a0ac", "text": "$\\frac{\\mathrm{m}}{2 \\alpha^2 \\mathrm{~d}}$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f502ee0e063d92682a2"}, {"id": "08a5a9", "text": "$\\frac{\\mathrm{md}}{2 \\alpha^2}$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f502ee0e063d92682a3"}, {"id": "8538d7", "text": "$2 \\mathrm{~m} \\alpha^2 \\mathrm{~d}$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f502ee0e063d92682a4"}, {"id": "f4d3d1", "text": "$\\frac{m \\alpha^2 \\mathrm{~d}}{2}$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f502ee0e063d92682a5"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f502ee0e063d92682a6", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0dfaa"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b476b"], "concepts": ["60e567dc499d1e49588f9cac"], "question": {"text": "A particle is released from height $S$ above the surface of the earth. At certain height its kinetic energy is three times its potential energy. The height from the surface of the earth and the speed of the particle at that instant are respectively."}, "options": [{"id": "1b2481", "text": "$\\frac{\\mathrm{S}}{2}, \\sqrt{\\frac{3 \\mathrm{gS}}{2}}$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f502ee0e063d92682a7"}, {"id": "a17cf6", "text": "$\\frac{\\mathrm{S}}{2}, \\frac{3 \\mathrm{gS}}{2}$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f502ee0e063d92682a8"}, {"id": "505f21", "text": "$\\frac{\\mathrm{S}}{4}, \\frac{3 \\mathrm{gS}}{2}$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f502ee0e063d92682a9"}, {"id": "a3a8b7", "text": "$\\frac{\\mathrm{S}}{4}, \\sqrt{\\frac{3 \\mathrm{gS}}{2}}$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f502ee0e063d92682aa"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f502ee0e063d92682ab", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0dfaa"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b476b"], "concepts": ["6117b64c478ae845c43c6820"], "question": {"text": "<p>As per the given figure, two blocks each of mass <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>250</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></math> are connected to a spring of spring constant <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>. If both are given velocity <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>v</mi></math> in opposite directions, then maximum elongation of the spring is</p><p><img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2F9be38da4-5bff-4329-8ffc-413921cd5f49-image.png?alt=media\" style=\"width: 200px; height: 47px;\" /></p>"}, "options": [{"id": "e2c790", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">v</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></mrow></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f502ee0e063d92682ac"}, {"id": "ce2784", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mi>v</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f502ee0e063d92682ad"}, {"id": "2cd843", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mi>v</mi><mn>4</mn></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f502ee0e063d92682ae"}, {"id": "cfa99d", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mi>v</mi><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f502ee0e063d92682af"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f502ee0e063d92682b0", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0dfaa"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b476b"], "concepts": ["60e40fd4f1ef260f84ed1e37"], "question": {"text": "A force acts on a <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mi>&#160;</mi><mi>kg</mi></math> object so that its position is given as a function of time as <math><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><msup><mrow><mi>t</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>.</mo></math> What is the work done by this force in first <math><mn>5</mn></math> seconds?"}, "options": [{"id": "76b964", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>875</mn><mi>&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f502ee0e063d92682b1"}, {"id": "1a0772", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>850</mn><mi>&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f502ee0e063d92682b2"}, {"id": "71fd1f", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>950</mn><mi>&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f502ee0e063d92682b3"}, {"id": "1e326f", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>900</mn><mi>&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f502ee0e063d92682b4"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f502ee0e063d92682b5", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0dfaa"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b476b"], "concepts": ["6117b8bd67dbe2603c3e85b3"], "question": {"text": "If the kinetic energy of a moving body becomes four times its initial kinetic energy, then the percentage change in its momentum will be:"}, "options": [{"id": "4ccf45", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>100</mn><mo>%</mo></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f502ee0e063d92682b6"}, {"id": "140d70", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>200</mn><mo>%</mo></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f502ee0e063d92682b7"}, {"id": "0997bf", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>300</mn><mo>%</mo></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f502ee0e063d92682b8"}, {"id": "f4edba", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>400</mn><mo>%</mo></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f502ee0e063d92682b9"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f502ee0e063d92682ba", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0dfaa"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b476b"], "concepts": ["60e2fb5666f9ce3f243b4f00"], "question": {"text": "<p>A bullet of mass <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>200</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></math> having initial kinetic energy <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>90</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi></math> is shot inside a long swimming pool as shown in the figure. If it&#39;s kinetic energy reduces&nbsp;to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>40</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi></math> within <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></math>, the minimum length of the pool, the bullet has&nbsp;to travel so that it completely comes to rest is</p><p><img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2F186e6a82-a8e4-44f3-aade-46cde3e0c363-image.png?alt=media\" style=\"width: 160px; height: 89px;\" /></p>"}, "options": [{"id": "4c0c2d", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>45</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f502ee0e063d92682bb"}, {"id": "50839b", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>90</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f502ee0e063d92682bc"}, {"id": "125164", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>125</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f502ee0e063d92682bd"}, {"id": "2b619f", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>25</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f502ee0e063d92682be"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f502ee0e063d92682bf", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0dfaa"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b476b"], "concepts": ["60e2fbdc66f9ce3f243b564c"], "question": {"text": "The potential energy function (in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi></math> ) of a particle in a region of space is given as <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>U</mi><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>z</mi></mrow></mfenced></math>. Here <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mo> </mo><mi>y</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>z</mi></math> are in meter. The magnitude of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi></math> - component of force (in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi></math> ) acting on the particle at point <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi><mo>(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mo> </mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mo> </mo><mn>3</mn><mo>)</mo><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math> is:"}, "options": [{"id": "4dae90", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f502ee0e063d92682c0"}, {"id": "8faa52", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>6</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f502ee0e063d92682c1"}, {"id": "59e4c2", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f502ee0e063d92682c2"}, {"id": "a29327", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>8</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f502ee0e063d92682c3"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f502ee0e063d92682c4", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0dfaa"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b476b"], "concepts": ["60e567dc499d1e49588f9cac"], "question": {"text": "Potential energy as a function of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>r</mi></math>&nbsp;is given by <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>U</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>A</mi><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>10</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mi>B</mi><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>5</mn></msup></mfrac></math>, where <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>r</mi></math>&nbsp;is the interatomic distance, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi></math> are positive constants. The equilibrium distance between the two atoms will be :"}, "options": [{"id": "a80e2f", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mfenced><mfrac><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi></mfrac></mfenced><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>5</mn></mfrac></msup></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f502ee0e063d92682c5"}, {"id": "487343", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mfenced><mfrac><mi>B</mi><mi>A</mi></mfrac></mfenced><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>5</mn></mfrac></msup></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f502ee0e063d92682c6"}, {"id": "f4846e", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mfenced><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>A</mi></mrow><mi>B</mi></mfrac></mfenced><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>5</mn></mfrac></msup></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f502ee0e063d92682c7"}, {"id": "bda915", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mfenced><mfrac><mi>B</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>A</mi></mrow></mfrac></mfenced><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>5</mn></mfrac></msup></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f502ee0e063d92682c8"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f502ee0e063d92682c9", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0dfaa"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b476b"], "concepts": ["60e40fd4f1ef260f84ed1e37"], "question": {"text": "A block of mass <math><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo></math> lying on a smooth horizontal surface, is attached to a spring (of negligible mass) of spring constant <math><mi>k</mi><mo>.</mo></math> The other end of the spring is fixed, as shown in the figure. The block is initially at rest in its equilibrium position. If now the block is pulled with a constant force <math><mi>F</mi><mo>,</mo></math> the maximum speed of the block is:<br /><br /><img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2Fgkvndhgfanlffeeyiwvnmuwttbylfqtrpnkjygclvmgynvyjiq.png?alt=media\" />"}, "options": [{"id": "622418", "text": "<math><mfrac><mrow><mi>F</mi></mrow><mrow><msqrt><mi>m</mi><mi>k</mi></msqrt></mrow></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f502ee0e063d92682ca"}, {"id": "b83ba0", "text": "<math><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>F</mi></mrow><mrow><msqrt><mi>m</mi><mi>k</mi></msqrt></mrow></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f502ee0e063d92682cb"}, {"id": "094255", "text": "<math><mfrac><mrow><mi>π</mi><mi>F</mi></mrow><mrow><msqrt><mi>m</mi><mi>k</mi></msqrt></mrow></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f502ee0e063d92682cc"}, {"id": "018113", "text": "<math><mfrac><mrow><mi>F</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>π</mi><msqrt><mi>m</mi><mi>k</mi></msqrt></mrow></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f502ee0e063d92682cd"}], "questionLabels": []}], "markingScheme": {"_id": "608283e223cf4b3ad8f125e6", "title": "JEE Single Correct", "correctAttempt": 4, "incorrectAttempt": -1, "createdAt": "2021-04-09T08:45:27.797Z", "updatedAt": "2021-07-05T05:39:15.785Z", "__v": 0, "updated_by": "6042252509c5bf34e8a2f178"}, "maximumAttemptLimit": 20, "linkedQuestions": [], "createdAt": "2026-04-14T14:29:36.191Z", "updatedAt": "2026-04-14T14:29:36.191Z", "__v": 0}, "position": 0, "_id": "69de4f502ee0e063d9268318"}, {"sectionId": {"_id": "69de4f502ee0e063d9268316", "title": "Physics Numerical", "sectionType": "normal", "subject": "607018ee404ae53194e73d90", "questions": [{"_id": "69de4f502ee0e063d92682f9", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0dfaa"], "topics": ["60e40fd5f1ef260f84ed1e96"], "concepts": ["60e567aa499d1e49588f95c3"], "question": {"text": "A force <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mover><mi>F</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfenced><mover><mi>i</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></math> acts on a particle in the <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi></math> direction where <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>F</mi></math> is in Newton and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi></math> is in meter. The work done by this force during a displacement from <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>=</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>0</mn></math>&nbsp;to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math>&nbsp;is _____&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi></math>."}, "options": [{"id": "012349", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f502ee0e063d92682fa"}, {"id": "e948b6", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f502ee0e063d92682fb"}, {"id": "a5a5d3", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f502ee0e063d92682fc"}, {"id": "144082", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f502ee0e063d92682fd"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f502ee0e063d92682fe", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0dfaa"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b476b"], "concepts": ["6117b8bd67dbe2603c3e85b3"], "question": {"text": "Two solids <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi></math> of mass <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>kg</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>kg</mi></math> respectively are moving with equal linear momentum. The ratio of their kinetic energies <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mfenced><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>.</mo><mi>E</mi><mo>.</mo></mrow></mfenced><mi>A</mi></msub><mo>:</mo><msub><mfenced><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>.</mo><mi>E</mi><mo>.</mo></mrow></mfenced><mi>B</mi></msub></math> will be <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mi>A</mi><mn>1</mn></mfrac><mo>,</mo></math>&nbsp;so the value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math> will be _________."}, "options": [{"id": "506187", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f502ee0e063d92682ff"}, {"id": "cde198", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f502ee0e063d9268300"}, {"id": "b8f5ae", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f502ee0e063d9268301"}, {"id": "5b61d2", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f502ee0e063d9268302"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f502ee0e063d9268303", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0dfaa"], "topics": ["60e2fb1f66f9ce3f243b4b68"], "concepts": ["60e2fb1f66f9ce3f243b4b2b"], "question": {"text": "A block of mass <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>kg</mi></math> starting from rest pulled up on a smooth incline plane making an angle of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>30</mn><mo>&#176;</mo></math> with horizontal with an effective acceleration of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></math>. The power delivered by the puling force at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></math> from the start is _____&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">W</mi></math>.<br />[Use <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>g</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></math>]<br />(Calculate the nearest integer value)"}, "options": [{"id": "2d5f4a", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f502ee0e063d9268304"}, {"id": "b60646", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f502ee0e063d9268305"}, {"id": "3c8c6d", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f502ee0e063d9268306"}, {"id": "6a8596", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f502ee0e063d9268307"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f502ee0e063d9268308", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0dfaa"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b476b"], "concepts": ["60e2fb5666f9ce3f243b4f00"], "question": {"text": "A <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>kg</mi></math> block moving at a speed of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>12</mn><msup><mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>ms</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math> compresses a spring through a distance <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>30</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi></math> when its speed is halved. The spring constant of the spring will be _____&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>Nm</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>"}, "options": [{"id": "7a19f6", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f502ee0e063d9268309"}, {"id": "53e0fc", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f502ee0e063d926830a"}, {"id": "e59a07", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f502ee0e063d926830b"}, {"id": "a2ba28", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f502ee0e063d926830c"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f502ee0e063d926830d", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0dfaa"], "topics": ["60e40fd5f1ef260f84ed1e96"], "concepts": ["60e40fd4f1ef260f84ed1e3c"], "question": {"text": "Two persons <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi></math> perform same amount of work in moving a body through a certain distance <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>d</mi></math> with application of forces acting at angles <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>45</mn><mo>&#176;</mo></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>60</mn><mo>&#176;</mo></math> with the direction of displacement respectively. The ratio of force applied by person <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math> to the force applied by person <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi></math> is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msqrt><mi>x</mi></msqrt></mfrac><mo>.</mo></math>&nbsp;The value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi></math> is _________."}, "options": [{"id": "d28975", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f502ee0e063d926830e"}, {"id": "857349", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f502ee0e063d926830f"}, {"id": "facdbd", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f502ee0e063d9268310"}, {"id": "f1ffb6", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f502ee0e063d9268311"}], "questionLabels": []}], "markingScheme": {"_id": "608283c623cf4b3ad8f125e5", "title": "JEE Numerical", "correctAttempt": 4, "incorrectAttempt": -1, "createdAt": "2021-04-09T08:45:27.797Z", "updatedAt": "2021-07-05T05:39:27.056Z", "__v": 0, "updated_by": "6042252509c5bf34e8a2f178"}, "maximumAttemptLimit": 5, "linkedQuestions": [], "createdAt": "2026-04-14T14:29:36.261Z", "updatedAt": "2026-04-14T14:29:36.261Z", "__v": 0}, "position": 1, "_id": "69de4f502ee0e063d9268319"}], "bonusSections": [], "packDetails": [], "paidFeatures": [], "tags": [], "timeRestrictionSlots": [], "createdAt": "2026-04-14T11:15:54.341Z", "updatedAt": "2026-04-17T04:57:58.162Z", "testType": "PYQs as Chapter Tests", "isResumeBufferAl